{
  "dom_id": "step-q352264",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Consider the finite region bounded by the curve $y=4{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}$ and the $x$-axis. Calculate the volume $V$ of the solid generated when this region is rotated $2\\pi $ radians about the $y$-axis. Do not round the answer.\n\n$V=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "First, we determine the points where the curve intersects the $x$-axis by solving the following equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(4-x) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solutions are $x=0$ and $x=4.$ So, we need to integrate from $x=0$ to $x=4.$ \n\nUsing the shell method, the volume of the solid can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =2\\pi {\\int }_{a}^{b}x\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{4}x(4{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{4}(4{x}^{3}-{x}^{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\pi {({x}^{4}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =2\\pi [({4}^{4}-\\frac{{4}^{5}}{5})-0] \\\\  & =2\\pi (256-\\frac{1024}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{512\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
